\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Calculated and measured grain-boundary chemistry as a function of dose. (a) Oxide composition on a metal (cation) basis, evaluated at the depth of the corresponding EDX line scan: 23, 30 and \SI {44}{nm} for 0, 0.5 and \SI {3.0}{\dpa }. (b) \ce {SiO2} volume fraction in the oxide, both at the same depths and averaged over the oxidized length of the boundary. (c) Ni concentration at the grain boundary before and after exposure; calculated profiles are convolved with a Gaussian of \SI {1}{nm} FWHM to match the quoted EDX probe diameter and are sampled at the depth of the measurement. Filled symbols with solid lines are calculations, open symbols with dashed lines the measurements of \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\textcite {deng}.}}{12}{}\protected@file@percent }
